</ul>
</nav>
<div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
<div class="mb-6">
<h2 class="text-lg font-bold">Visibility</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Who outside testorg can read this component</p>
</div>
<div class="space-y-6 max-w-2xl">

<div class="p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
<dl class="text-sm space-y-3">
<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
<dt class="text-gray-500">Visible outside the organisation</dt>
<dd><span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium bg-green-100 text-green-800">Public</span></dd>
</div>
<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
<dt class="text-gray-500">This component's own setting</dt>
<dd><span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium bg-gray-100 text-gray-700">Private</span></dd>
</div>
<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
<dt class="text-gray-500">Organisation <a href="/orgs/testorg/settings/visibility" class="underline hover:text-gray-900">testorg</a></dt>
<dd><span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium bg-green-100 text-green-800">Public</span></dd>
</div>
</dl>
</div>
<div class="p-3 rounded-md bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 text-sm text-amber-900">
          This component is public through the organisation: testorg is public, so every
          component it publishes is visible to anyone, even without signing in. Setting this component to private
          does not make it private while the organisation is public. Change that in the
          <a href="/orgs/testorg/settings/visibility" class="underline font-medium">organisation's visibility settings</a>.
        </div>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
<strong>Public is read-only.</strong> A public component is listed on the public registry
  pages, with its readme, versions and manifest, for anyone to see, <em>including people who are
  not signed in</em>. Anyone signed in to Forest can also resolve and download it. Publishing,
  unpublishing and every other change still need membership of the organisation. The
  organisation's releases, destinations, members and settings are not shared.
</p>
<form method="POST" action="/orgs/testorg/projects/widget/settings/visibility" class="space-y-3">
<input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="test-csrf">
<fieldset class="space-y-2">
<legend class="sr-only">Visibility of testorg/widget</legend>
<label class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm">
<input type="radio" name="visibility" value="private" checked class="mt-0.5">
<span><span class="font-medium">Private</span> — only members of the organisation can read it.</span>
</label>
<label class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm">
<input type="radio" name="visibility" value="public" class="mt-0.5">
<span><span class="font-medium">Public</span> — anyone can see it, even without signing in, and anyone signed in can use it. Read-only.</span>
</label>
</fieldset>
<button type="submit" class="px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-md hover:bg-gray-800">Save visibility</button>
</form>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
